  "slope_claim": "The STRUCTURE is universal across the panel: in every model the bare-assignment (neutral) and task-devotion arms collapse to high collateral harm while the steward (collective-objective) arm holds a low floor -- assignment, not instruction content, carries the effect. The MAGNITUDE of the assignment contrast scales with capability rather than along a single monotone line: across two independent frontier vendors in a tiered design the neutral-vs-steward odds ratio rises from roughly 11x in the weak edge model (Gemma-3 12B) to ~50-120x in capable cloud models (DeepSeek-V4 Flash), because a more capable model both follows the steward objective more cleanly (lower steward floor) and executes the assigned-patient grab more completely (higher devotion CHR). The relationship is monotone in DIRECTION (capability sharpens the contrast) but NOT a clean monotone capability curve in level: the smallest edge models (Qwen-3.5 0.8B/2B) invert the steward floor entirely (they grab MORE under the steward objective than under devotion, an OR < 1), reflecting an inability to represent the collective objective at all rather than safety. We therefore report the universal structure as the primary claim and the capability scaling as a directional, vendor-replicated trend, not a fitted scalar slope."
}
